                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ceea45da-7e04-388a-989f-5687ea4fd71e",
                        "entry_id": "d5b37cbd-e6b0-37b8-a234-7124e0954012",
                        "glosses": [
                            "to wear to rags, to fray, to tear"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4599e7d2-448c-4159-9ec4-eb334692a939",
                                "sense_id": "ceea45da-7e04-388a-989f-5687ea4fd71e",
                                "text": "истрепа́ть не́рвы кому́-либо",
                                "translation": "wear out [fray] someone's nerves",
                                "english": "wear out [fray] someone's nerves"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c02eaf97-66b9-4e37-b747-2ef12a9ad6f7",
                                "sense_id": "ceea45da-7e04-388a-989f-5687ea4fd71e",
                                "text": "Жизнь до тако́й сте́пени истрепа́ла его́, что не оста́вила на нём никако́го при́знака дворя́нского сы́на, ни мале́йшего сле́да того́, что и он был когда́-то в университе́те и что и к нему́ то́же бы́ло обращено́ воспита́тельное сло́во нау́ки.",
                                "translation": "Life has so jaded him that there is no sign now of his gentry birth, not the faintest indication that he once attended the university and had addressed to him the improving word of science.",
                                "english": "Life has so jaded him that there is no sign now of his gentry birth, not the faintest indication that he once attended the university and had addressed to him the improving word of science."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
